1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:04,200
Vitals World — a public ward
on Solana devnet.

2
00:00:04,600 --> 00:00:08,400
Each country shaded by people per doctor
— World Bank/WHO.

3
00:00:08,800 --> 00:00:12,400
Ethiopia: 1 doctor per 6,990 people
(World Bank, 2023).

4
00:00:12,800 --> 00:00:15,800
The ring: 1 patient from Ethiopia
in a bed right now.

5
00:00:18,200 --> 00:00:23,400
The years 2005 → 2023:
the map follows the slider.

6
00:00:25,600 --> 00:00:27,600
The census: 31 shifts —
/api/ward counts anchored leaves.

7
00:00:28,100 --> 00:00:31,800
Three patients in beds, three countries —
each row: take a shift.

8
00:00:32,300 --> 00:00:36,500
Maria Bautista, 69, from the Philippines —
a simulated patient.

9
00:00:37,100 --> 00:00:41,500
One press takes the head — declared
on chain before it is played.

10
00:00:42,300 --> 00:00:45,300
On her chart, under your key —
the lease runs about 10 minutes.

11
00:00:45,700 --> 00:00:49,500
The case's own question, pressed —
her scripted answer appears.

12
00:00:51,500 --> 00:00:56,700
Two orders: oxygen,
then source control.

13
00:00:57,900 --> 00:01:02,500
Oxygen on: the saturation climbs,
the monitor says Improving.

14
00:01:05,700 --> 00:01:10,300
The chart: every order at its clock time,
earlier shifts included.

15
00:01:12,300 --> 00:01:15,900
Hand over: the shift reduces to a leaf,
anchored on Solana devnet.

16
00:01:16,500 --> 00:01:20,300
Handed over: her chain is 4 shifts long.
Next: the receipt.

17
00:01:21,200 --> 00:01:24,200
The receipt: what was asked and ordered,
at its time.

18
00:01:28,100 --> 00:01:31,700
6 of 40: deterministic marks,
row by row, the case's own rubric.

19
00:01:32,100 --> 00:01:35,100
Check it yourself: the devnet explorer,
the tape to download.

20
00:01:35,500 --> 00:01:38,900
The addresses: patient, case, slot,
leaf, run hash, the player's key.

21
00:01:39,800 --> 00:01:42,600
The transaction on Solana Explorer —
a witness that is not us.

22
00:01:43,200 --> 00:01:47,000
The program's own log:
“anchored at leaf 31”.

23
00:01:47,800 --> 00:01:52,000
A second key, the same bed:
“chart rebuilt from 4 anchored shifts”.

24
00:01:52,600 --> 00:01:56,200
The chart carries every earlier order,
rebuilt from the chain.

25
00:01:57,100 --> 00:02:02,300
A patient who left: she went home —
two shifts, two receipts.

26
00:02:03,300 --> 00:02:05,900
Every case the ward holds — provisional,
each badged NOT REVIEWED.

27
00:02:06,300 --> 00:02:09,100
Some cases are endemic to a country —
this one: dengue, PHL.

28
00:02:10,500 --> 00:02:16,500
A review run: read the case —
nothing recorded, nobody in a bed.

29
00:02:17,600 --> 00:02:20,400
Back on the globe: 32 shifts —
the one you watched among them.

30
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:25,200
Vitals World · world.vitals.academy
a public ward on Solana devnet
patients simulated, the shortage is not

